  "placement_rules": [
    "Every bot has exactly one primary division owner.",
    "Cross-domain bots may declare secondary collaborator divisions instead of being duplicated.",
    "Placement is scored from display name, category, description, target users and capabilities.",
    "A bot is only a move candidate when another division materially outscores its current division and the evidence is explainable.",
    "Low-confidence cases stay in place and are flagged for review.",
    "Shared infrastructure belongs in CommandCore, DreamAIInfra, DreamAgents, DreamAutomation, DreamFlow, DreamData or DreamCodeLab when broadly reusable rather than copied into domain divisions.",
    "Revenue opportunity does not determine placement; domain ownership does. Sales, payments and finance bots support other divisions through shared services rather than absorbing their domain bots."
